Subject: Accept downlinks in regions station does not know

v2.0.6 sets region = 0 for regions it does not know (anything but EU868, IL915,
KR920, AS923-1, US915 and AU915). region == 0 also means "no router_config
yet", so every downlink in those regions was dropped. The gate now tests
txpow, which is 0 only until router_config sets it, so downlinks that arrive
before router_config are still dropped in every region. Side effect: a
router_config with max_eirp 0 makes station drop every downlink.

diff --git a/src/s2e.c b/src/s2e.c
index 6540415..22a68a3 100644
--- a/src/s2e.c
+++ b/src/s2e.c
@@ -1792,7 +1792,7 @@ int s2e_onMsg (s2ctx_t* s2ctx, char* json, ujoff_t jsonlen) {
         LOG(MOD_S2E|ERROR, "Parsing of JSON message failed - ignored");
         return 1;   // return fail? would trigger a reconnect
     }
-    if( s2ctx->region == 0 && (msgtype == J_dnmsg || msgtype == J_dnsched || msgtype == J_dnframe) ) {
+    if( s2ctx->txpow == 0 && (msgtype == J_dnmsg || msgtype == J_dnsched || msgtype == J_dnframe) ) {
         // Might happen if messages are still queued
         LOG(MOD_S2E|WARNING, "Received '%.*s' before 'router_config' - dropped", D.str.len, D.str.beg);
         return 1;
